  "description": "bmp581 0.2.1 requires the owner-task model and the project's i2c0 is guarded: it is held back (KB-RES-018), 0.2.0 is taken and its known vulnerability is warned (KB-UPG-W03).",
  "expect": {
    "errors": [],
    "files": {
      "CMakePresets.json": "{\n  \"configurePresets\": [\n    {\n      \"binaryDir\": \"${sourceDir}/build/owner-gate\",\n      \"cacheVariables\": {\n        \"KB_DRIVER_BMP581_DIR\": \"${sourceDir}/external/drivers/driver-bmp581\",\n        \"KB_ENABLE_BMP581\": \"ON\",\n        \"KB_MCU\": \"ESP32\",\n        \"KB_PARTS\": \"utils;rtos;interfaces;handlers\",\n        \"KB_RTOS\": \"FREERTOS\"\n      },\n      \"displayName\": \"kb image owner-gate\",\n      \"name\": \"owner-gate\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"version\": 6\n}\n",
      "kb-fetch.sh": "#!/bin/sh\n# kb-fetch.sh: adds kb-core, the MCU port and the drivers of the image \"owner-gate\" to this git repository as\n# submodules under external/, each checked out at its tag (a kb-core development revision: at its commit) and\n# verified against the commit in kb-image.lock.yml (ADR-0012, ADR-0014). A tag that moved is refused. No branch\n# is recorded in .gitmodules and nothing is fetched recursively. Rerunning it is safe. Written by kb resolve.\n#\n#   sh kb-fetch.sh            add or update every pin\n#   sh kb-fetch.sh --verify   only check that every submodule is at its pinned commit\nset -eu\n\nmode=add\nif [ \"${1:-}\" = \"--verify\" ]; then mode=verify; fi\ntop=$(git rev-parse --show-toplevel 2>/dev/null) || { echo \"kb-fetch: run this inside a git repository\" >&2; exit 1; }\ncd \"$top\"\n\ndie() {\n  printf 'kb-fetch: error: %s\\n' \"$*\" >&2\n  exit 1\n}\n\n# pin <path> <url> <tag, empty for a commit pin> <commit>\npin() {\n  path=$1 url=$2 tag=$3 want=$4\n  if [ \"$mode\" = verify ]; then\n    [ -e \"$path/.git\" ] || die \"$path is missing; run without --verify\"\n  else\n    if [ ! -e \"$path/.git\" ]; then\n      git submodule add --quiet \"$url\" \"$path\" || die \"cannot add $url\"\n    fi\n    if [ -n \"$tag\" ]; then\n      git -C \"$path\" fetch --quiet origin \"+refs/tags/$tag:refs/tags/$tag\" || die \"cannot fetch $tag of $url\"\n      got=$(git -C \"$path\" rev-parse \"refs/tags/$tag^{commit}\")\n      [ \"$got\" = \"$want\" ] || die \"$path: tag $tag points at $got, expected $want (the tag moved; it is not used)\"\n    else\n      git -C \"$path\" fetch --quiet origin \"$want\" || die \"cannot fetch commit $want of $url\"\n    fi\n    git -C \"$path\" -c advice.detachedHead=false checkout --quiet \"$want\"\n    git config -f .gitmodules --unset \"submodule.$path.branch\" 2>/dev/null || true\n    git add .gitmodules \"$path\"\n  fi\n  head=$(git -C \"$path\" rev-parse HEAD)\n  [ \"$head\" = \"$want\" ] || die \"$path is at $head, expected $want\"\n  printf 'kb-fetch: %s at %s (%s)\\n' \"$path\" \"${tag:-commit}\" \"$want\"\n}\n\n# kb-core 0.4.1\npin 'external/kb-core' 'https://github.com/kokeb-labs/kb-core.git' 'v0.4.1' '83518d7664b87cabd87681c5835cc32c4c78ab49'\n# driver bmp581 0.2.0\npin 'external/drivers/driver-bmp581' 'https://github.com/kokeb-labs-drivers/driver-bmp581.git' 'v0.2.0' '05c0484e290901d646347a15279de7afbb87ba13'\n\nif [ \"$mode\" = add ]; then\n  echo \"kb-fetch: done; review with git status and commit the submodules\"\nfi\n",
      "kb-image.lock.yml": "# kb image lock (schema 1), written by kb resolve: do not edit.\n{\n  \"buses\": [\n    {\n      \"devices\": [\n        \"bmp581\"\n      ],\n      \"kind\": \"i2c\",\n      \"model\": \"guarded\",\n      \"name\": \"i2c0\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"cmake\": {\n    \"KB_ENABLE_BMP581\": \"ON\",\n    \"KB_MCU\": \"ESP32\",\n    \"KB_PARTS\": \"utils;rtos;interfaces;handlers\",\n    \"KB_RTOS\": \"FREERTOS\"\n  },\n  \"drivers\": [\n    {\n      \"authors\": [\n        \"The driver-bmp581 authors\"\n      ],\n      \"commit\": \"05c0484e290901d646347a15279de7afbb87ba13\",\n      \"folder\": \"driver-bmp581\",\n      \"kind\": \"release\",\n      \"license\": \"MIT\",\n      \"name\": \"bmp581\",\n      \"repo\": \"kokeb-labs-drivers/driver-bmp581\",\n      \"tag\": \"v0.2.0\",\n      \"version\": \"0.2.0\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"image\": \"owner-gate\",\n  \"kb_core\": {\n    \"authors\": [\n      \"The kb-core authors\"\n    ],\n    \"commit\": \"83518d7664b87cabd87681c5835cc32c4c78ab49\",\n    \"kind\": \"release\",\n    \"license\": \"MIT\",\n    \"repo\": \"kokeb-labs/kb-core\",\n    \"tag\": \"v0.4.1\",\n    \"version\": \"0.4.1\"\n  },\n  \"mcu\": {\n    \"family\": \"esp32\",\n    \"target\": \"esp32\"\n  },\n  \"parts\": [\n    \"utils\",\n    \"rtos\",\n    \"interfaces\",\n    \"handlers\"\n  ],\n  \"ports\": [\n    {\n      \"commit\": \"83518d7664b87cabd87681c5835cc32c4c78ab49\",\n      \"in_tree\": true,\n      \"name\": \"esp32\",\n      \"path\": \"components/ports/esp32\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"rtos\": \"freertos\",\n  \"schema\": 1\n}\n",
      "kb-image.yml": "# kb-image.yml: the selection of one firmware build (schema 1, docs/design/assembler.md).\n# Written by an upgrade (kb upgrade or the configurator); resolve it with: kb resolve kb-image.yml\nschema: 1\nimage: \"owner-gate\"\nkb_core: {version: \"0.4.1\"}\nmcu: {family: \"esp32\"}\ndrivers:\n  - {name: \"bmp581\", version: \"0.2.0\"}\nbuses:\n  i2c0: {model: \"guarded\", devices: [\"bmp581\"]}\n",
      "kb-upgrade.md": "# Upgrade report: owner-gate\n\nkb-core 0.4.1 to 0.4.1, MCU esp32/esp32, RTOS freertos. Release candidates not picked unless named.\n\n1 of 2 component(s) change.\n\n| Component | From | To | Change | Breaking | Newest release | Newer rc | Known vulnerabilities |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| kb-core | 0.4.1 | 0.4.1 | none | no | 0.4.1 | 0.5.0-rc.1 | none |\n| bmp581 | 0.1.0 | 0.2.0 | minor | yes | 1.0.0 | - | CVE-2026-0001 -> GHSA-bmp5-0002 |\n\n## Breaking changes\n\n- bmp581 0.1.0 -> 0.2.0: read its release notes and CHANGELOG before building: https://github.com/kokeb-labs-drivers/driver-bmp581/releases/tag/v0.2.0\n\n## Held back\n\n- bmp581 1.0.0: needs a newer kb-core (KB-RES-014)\n- bmp581 0.2.1: requires an owner-task bus (KB-RES-018)\n\n## Known vulnerabilities\n\n- fixed by this upgrade: CVE-2026-0001 (bmp581)\n- still present: GHSA-bmp5-0002 (bmp581 0.2.0)\n\n## Warnings\n\n- KB-UPG-W01 bmp581: breaking change\n- KB-UPG-W02 bmp581: newer version held back\n- KB-UPG-W03 bmp581: known vulnerabilities remain\n\n## Next steps\n\n1. Review the changes to `kb-image.yml` and `kb-image.lock.yml` with `git diff`.\n2. Run `sh kb-fetch.sh` to move every submodule to its new tag, then build and run your tests.\n3. Check the compatibility of the new set: a tested version set, or an untested combination.\n",
      "kb_image.cmake": "# kb image owner-gate: written by kb resolve from kb-image.yml (schema 1); do not edit.\n# kb-core 0.4.1 at 83518d7664b87cabd87681c5835cc32c4c78ab49, MCU esp32/esp32, RTOS freertos.\nset(KB_MCU \"ESP32\")\nset(KB_RTOS \"FREERTOS\")\nset(KB_PARTS \"utils;rtos;interfaces;handlers\")\nset(KB_ENABLE_BMP581 ON)\nset(KB_DRIVER_BMP581_DIR \"${CMAKE_CURRENT_LIST_DIR}/external/drivers/driver-bmp581\")\n"
    },
